spu_channels: the "[spurs-pm] poll" print only under SPURS_PM_TRACE.

The poll count restarts with every policy-module run, so the "first four polls" print fired on every run: several lines
a frame in Resistance 3, interleaved with the game's own output. The exit-to-kernel print next to it is already gated by
SPURS_PM_TRACE; the poll print now is too.

Test: scripted run: no "[spurs-pm] poll" line without SPURS_PM_TRACE.

Upstream: not proposed yet.

---

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
index ec5a653..f9433e9 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
@@ -2172,6 +2172,9 @@ void spu_indirect_branch(spu_context* ctx)
              * (The host scheduler admits bounded workers; this service does not preempt.) */
+            /* Print gated like exit-to-kernel above: the count restarts with
+             * every policy run, so "the first few" is several lines a frame. */
             unsigned n = ++g_spurs_pm_polls;
-            if (n <= 4 || (n % 4096) == 0)
+            { static SPU_THREAD_LOCAL int s_t = -1; if (s_t < 0) s_t = getenv("SPURS_PM_TRACE") ? 1 : 0;
+              if (s_t && (n <= 4 || (n % 4096) == 0))
                 fprintf(stderr, "[spurs-pm] poll #%u (r3=0x%08X) -> continue\n",
-                        n, ctx->gpr[3]._u32[0]);
+                        n, ctx->gpr[3]._u32[0]); }
             ctx->gpr[3] = spu_make_preferred_u32(0);
